{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go | sed -n '1620,1645p'; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | tail -13; rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic\\\\(' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go; pose recurrence-check --tolerant --window-days 14\"","aggregated_output":"  1620\t\tsummary := &validationSummary{Outcome: run.Outcome}\n  1621\t\tfor _, check := range run.Checks {\n  1622\t\t\tcommand := strings.TrimSpace(check.Program + \" \" + strings.Join(check.Args, \" \"))\n  1623\t\t\tif check.Outcome != \"skipped\" && command != \"\" {\n  1624\t\t\t\tsummary.Commands = append(summary.Commands, command)\n  1625\t\t\t}\n  1626\t\t\tline := \"- [\" + check.Outcome + \"] \" + check.ID\n  1627\t\t\tswitch {\n  1628\t\t\tcase check.SkipReason != \"\":\n  1629\t\t\t\tline += \" (\" + check.SkipReason + \")\"\n  1630\t\t\tcase check.DurationSeconds > 0:\n  1631\t\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" (%.1fs)\", check.DurationSeconds)\n  1632\t\t\t}\n  1633\t\t\tif check.ExitCode != nil {\n  1634\t\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" exit=%d\", *check.ExitCode)\n  1635\t\t\t}\n  1636\t\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, line)\n  1637\t\t}\n  1638\t\t// The report records the run's verdict too, built from the outcome rather\n  1639\t\t// than copied from the printed line, so the recorded evidence keeps its\n  1640\t\t// shape while the terminal is free to change.\n  1641\t\tif run.Counts.OptionalFailed > 0 {\n  1642\t\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, fmt.Sprintf(\"Warning: %d optional check(s) failed.\", run.Counts.OptionalFailed))\n  1643\t\t}\n  1644\t\tswitch run.Outcome {\n  1645\t\tcase \"fail\":\n   250\t\n   251\t### Files and modules changed\n   252\t`pose-mcp/internal/cli` (validate, its scope selection, its result fields and the help catalogue), `pose-mcp/internal/pose` (the delivery reading of the result), the manual in English and pt-BR with their embedded copies, this spec and its ADR.\n   253\t\n   254\t### Validation executed\n   255\tSee the execution log: the package tests with mutation checks, the full `go test ./...` and the strict matrix with 236 of 236 checks.\n   256\t\n   257\t### Residual risks\n   258\tAn instance that declares a module self-contained while its checks read files outside it would carry a stale result. The declaration is explicit and documented, and the default stays the full fallback.\n   259\t\n   260\t### Follow-ups\n   261\t- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   262\t- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\nrecurrence.flapping_keys=0\nrecurrence.resolved_clusters=0\nrecurrence.window_days=14\nrecurrence.threshold=3\nrecurrence.records_scanned=432\nrecurrence.flagged_keys=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
