{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/material_binding.go; sed -n '127,242p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry_test.go; rg -n 'func Main|PrintContributorFailureHint|noteUsage' pose-mcp/internal/cli/main.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/contribut*.go; sed -n '1,75p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"package pose\n\nimport (\n\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"path\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// Validation evidence binds to the material it validated (spec\n// pose-validation-evidence-material-binding, ADR\n// validation-evidence-binds-to-validated-material). A commit whose every\n// changed path is a derived administrative record does not change what the\n// checks exercised, so it does not move the material digest.\n\n// engineVersion is the running engine, registered by the binaries (internal/pose\n// stays importable on its own). It is part of every material digest, so a new\n// engine never inherits evidence the previous one produced.\nvar engineVersion = \"unregistered\"\n\n// SetEngineVersion registers the running engine for material digests.\nfunc SetEngineVersion(v string) { engineVersion = v }\n\n// administrativeDirs is the closed list of derived-record directories. It is\n// owned by the engine; adding a class is a contract change that needs an ADR.\nvar administrativeDirs = []string{\".pose/indexes/\", \".pose/results/\", \".pose/state/\", \".pose/assessments/\"}\n\n// materialIndexes are files inside an administrative directory that still\n// change what the checks demand.\nvar materialIndexes = map[string]bool{\".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\": true}\n\n// IsAdministrativePath reports whether p is a derived administrative record.\nfunc IsAdministrativePath(p string) bool {\n\tif p == \"\" || p != path.Clean(p) || strings.HasPrefix(p, \"/\") || strings.HasPrefix(p, \"../\") {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tif materialIndexes[p] {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tif !recordExtensions[strings.ToLower(path.Ext(p))] {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\tfor _, dir := range administrativeDirs {\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(p, dir) {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif rest, ok := strings.CutPrefix(p, \".pose/\"); ok {\n\t\tif i := strings.Index(rest, \"/\"); i > 0 && strings.HasPrefix(rest[:i], \"review-\") {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// recordExtensions are the data formats a derived record is written in. Code or\n// a script stored in a class is material: that keeps a source file moved or\n// copied into a class from hiding its later edits. A copied data file stays\n// indistinguishable from a record; a check that reads data out of a derived-record\n// directory is outside this contract (ADR validation-evidence-binds-to-validated-material).\nvar recordExtensions = map[string]bool{\".json\": true, \".jsonl\": true, \".ndjson\": true, \".md\": true, \".txt\": true, \".log\": true, \".transcript\": true}\n\n// TreeEntry is one entry of the validated head's tree.\ntype TreeEntry struct{ Mode, Blob string }\n\nfunc regularMode(mode string) bool { return mode == \"100644\" || mode == \"100755\" }\n\n// MaterialInputs are what a material digest is computed from: the paths a change\n// set names (both sides of a rename, and the validation matrix) and the\n// destinations of renames. They are stored with the set so the digest can be\n// recomputed against the current tree without the commits' own records.\ntype MaterialInputs struct {\n\tNames []string `json:\"names\"`\n\tMoved []string `json:\"moved,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// MaterialInputsOf derives the inputs from per-commit path records. They must\n// be unmerged: folding a create and a later rename into one creation would hide\n// that the file moved into a class.\nfunc MaterialInputsOf(paths []ObservedPath) MaterialInputs {\n\tnames := map[string]bool{\".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\": true}\n\tmoved := map[string]bool{}\n\tfor _, p := range paths {\n\t\tfor _, name := range []string{p.Path, p.OldPath, p.NewPath} {\n\t\t\tif name != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tnames[name] = true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\t// A rename destination is material whatever directory it lands in:\n\t\t// otherwise moving a source file into a class would hide its later edits.\n\t\tif p.OldPath != \"\" && p.NewPath != \"\" {\n\t\t\tmoved[p.NewPath] = true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tin := MaterialInputs{}\n\tfor name := range names {\n\t\tin.Names = append(in.Names, name)\n\t}\n\tfor name := range moved {\n\t\tin.Moved = append(in.Moved, name)\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(in.Names)\n\tsort.Strings(in.Moved)\n\treturn in\n}\n\n// MaterialSetDigest digests the head state of the material a change set\nfunc TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule(t *testing.T) {\n\tf := newCarryFixture(t, \"\")\n\tbase := f.baseline()\n\tf.write(\"a/changed.go\", \"package a\\n\")\n\thead := f.commit(\"change a\")\n\tcode, out, run := f.validate(\"--carry\")\n\tif code != 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"exit=%d %s\", code, out)\n\t}\n\tif got := strings.Join(f.ran(), \",\"); got != \"a\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"executed modules = %q, want only a\", got)\n\t}\n\tif run.Carry == nil || !run.Carry.Used || run.Carry.BaseHead != base {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"carry = %+v, want used from %s\", run.Carry, base)\n\t}\n\tif b := checkOf(run, \"b\"); b.Outcome != \"pass\" || b.CarriedFrom != base || b.CarriedGeneratedAt == \"\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"b = %+v, want a pass carried from %s\", b, base)\n\t}\n\tif a := checkOf(run, \"a\"); a.CarriedFrom != \"\" || a.Outcome != \"pass\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a = %+v, want executed\", a)\n\t}\n\tif run.GitHead != head || run.Counts.Carried != 1 || run.Counts.Executed != 1 || run.Counts.Passed != 2 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"head=%s counts=%+v\", run.GitHead, run.Counts)\n\t}\n\tif run.EngineVersion == \"\" {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"engine_version must be recorded\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestCarryKeepsTheOriginalHeadAcrossChainedCarries(t *testing.T) {\n\tf := newCarryFixture(t, \"\")\n\tbase := f.baseline()\n\tf.write(\"a/one.go\", \"package a\\n\")\n\tf.commit(\"change a\")\n\tif code, out, _ := f.validate(\"--carry\"); code != 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"exit=%d %s\", code, out)\n\t}\n\tf.commit(\"record again\")\n\tf.write(\"a/two.go\", \"package a\\n\")\n\tf.commit(\"change a again\")\n\t_, _, run := f.validate(\"--carry\")\n\tif b := checkOf(run, \"b\"); b.CarriedFrom != base {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"b carried from %q, want the head it ran at %s\", b.CarriedFrom, base)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestCarryKeepsACarriedFailureAFailure(t *testing.T) {\n\tf := newCarryFixture(t, \"\")\n\tf.write(\"b/fail\", \"x\\n\")\n\tf.commit(\"b fails\")\n\tif code, _, _ := f.validate(); code == 0 {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"baseline with a failing b must fail\")\n\t}\n\tf.commit(\"record\")\n\tf.write(\"a/changed.go\", \"package a\\n\")\n\tf.commit(\"change a\")\n\tcode, _, run := f.validate(\"--carry\")\n\tif code == 0 || run.Outcome != \"fail\" || checkOf(run, \"b\").Outcome != \"fail\" || checkOf(run, \"b\").CarriedFrom == \"\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"exit=%d outcome=%s b=%+v, want the carried failure to fail the run\", code, run.Outcome, checkOf(run, \"b\"))\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun(t *testing.T) {\n\tcases := []struct {\n\t\tname   string\n\t\tmutate func(f *carryFixture)\n\t\treason string\n\t}{\n\t\t{\"no base\", func(f *carryFixture) {}, \"no canonical result\"},\n\t\t{\"matrix changed\", func(f *carryFixture) {\n\t\t\tf.baseline()\n\t\t\traw, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(f.root, \".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\"))\n\t\t\tf.write(\".pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\", strings.Replace(string(raw), `\"strict\"`, `\"strict\" `, 1))\n\t\t\tf.commit(\"matrix\")\n\t\t}, \"matrix\"},\n\t\t{\"dirty worktree\", func(f *carryFixture) {\n\t\t\tf.baseline()\n\t\t\tf.write(\"a/dirty.go\", \"package a\\n\")\n\t\t}, \"working copy\"},\n\t\t{\"base not an ancestor\", func(f *carryFixture) {\n\t\t\tf.baseline()\n\t\t\traw, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(f.root, carryResults))\n\t\t\tvar run map[string]any\n\t\t\t_ = json.Unmarshal(raw, &run)\n\t\t\trun[\"git_head\"] = strings.Repeat(\"0\", 40)\n\t\t\tout, _ := json.Marshal(run)\n\t\t\tf.write(carryResults, string(out))\n\t\t\tf.commit(\"forged base\")\n\t\t}, \"ancestor\"},\n\t\t{\"base without engine version\", func(f *carryFixture) {\n\t\t\tf.baseline()\n\t\t\traw, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(f.root, carryResults))\n\t\t\tvar run map[string]any\n\t\t\t_ = json.Unmarshal(raw, &run)\n\t\t\tdelete(run, \"engine_version\")\n\t\t\tout, _ := json.Marshal(run)\n\t\t\tf.write(carryResults, string(out))\n\t\t\tf.commit(\"old base\")\n\t\t}, \"engine\"},\n\t}\n\tfor _, tc := range cases {\n\t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tf := newCarryFixture(t, \"\")\n\t\t\ttc.mutate(f)\n\t\t\t_, out, run := f.validate(\"--carry\")\n\t\t\tif got := strings.Join(f.ran(), \",\"); got != \"a,b\" {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"executed = %q, want a full run; out=%s\", got, out)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif run.Carry == nil || run.Carry.Used || !strings.Contains(run.Carry.Reason, tc.reason) {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"carry = %+v, want unused with a reason naming %q\", run.Carry, tc.reason)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestCarryRootChangeRunsEverythingUnlessSelfContained(t *testing.T) {\nrg: pose-mcp/internal/cli/main.go: No such file or directory (os error 2)\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute.go:751:// PrintContributorFailureHint emits an actionable hint when a check/lint/close failure occurs and contributor mode is active.\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute.go:752:func PrintContributorFailureHintIn(files posepkg.Files, root string, w io.Writer, loc cliLocale) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute.go:764:// PrintContributorFailureHint reads and writes the filesystem directly; PrintContributorFailureHintIn takes the\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute.go:766:func PrintContributorFailureHint(root string, w io.Writer, loc cliLocale) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute.go:767:\tPrintContributorFailureHintIn(posepkg.NativeFiles(), root, w, loc)\npose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go:27:func Main(args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute_hints_test.go:18:\tPrintContributorFailureHint(temp, &buf, \"en\")\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute_hints_test.go:42:\tPrintContributorFailureHint(temp, &buf, \"en\")\npose-mcp/internal/cli/contribute_hints_test.go:49:\tPrintContributorFailureHint(temp, &buf, \"pt-BR\")\n# Adversarial corpus\n\nSpec: `pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus`. Test: `adversarial_corpus_test.go`.\n\nEvery gate POSE adds against mechanical compliance can itself be satisfied\nmechanically. Each row is the cheapest formal satisfaction of one gate. An\n`enforced` case fails the build when the shortcut works again; a `known-gap`\ncase fails the build when the gap closes, so it cannot close or reopen\nsilently; a `planned` case belongs to a spec not yet delivered and gains code\nbefore that spec closes; a `delegated` case is enforced by a test in another\npackage, named in the row, whose existence the corpus checks.\n\nThis corpus belongs to developing POSE's governance. It adds no checklist to an\nadopting project's features.\n\n| Case | Status | Shortcut it refuses | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `human-label-without-confirmation` | enforced | An agent writes and applies a review under `human:<name>`; the record reads as a human review | pose-review-attribution-roles |\n| `declared-independent-prefix` | enforced | `agent:independent-*` under declared assurance reads as authenticated separation | pose-review-assurance-disclosure |\n| `confirmation-reused-for-edited-content` | enforced | A confirmation recorded for one set of conclusions is kept after they change | pose-review-attribution-roles |\n| `unknown-recorded-as-satisfied` | enforced | An obligation the engine could not observe is reported as satisfied | pose-obligation-contract |\n| `legacy-blocker-gains-an-actor` | enforced | A blocker known only as text is given an invented recipient | pose-obligation-contract |\n| `blocked-counted-as-resolved` | enforced | Operational waiting counts as a resolved outcome in success metrics | pose-blocked-semantics-alignment |\n| `flat-specs-share-one-journal` | enforced | Two flat specs record amendments in one shared journal | pose-flat-spec-amendments |\n| `local-metadata-read-as-published` | enforced | A locally read version is presented as a proven publication | pose-public-claims-publication-provenance |\n| `invented-trace-test-ref` | known-gap | A requirement trace cites a test that does not exist and `lint-spec --strict` passes (follow-up 097 of pose-abm-design-basis) | pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus |\n| `unavailable-producer-reads-as-empty` | enforced | A producer fails and Attention reports zero obligations as a complete answer | pose-obligation-projection |\n| `trivial-change-raises-a-request` | enforced | A trivial change or an already-authorized instruction produces an ActionRequest | pose-action-requests |\n| `declined-approval-satisfies` | enforced | A declined approval, or a cancellation without authority, releases a gate | pose-action-request-resolution |\n| `closeout-plan-fills-judgment` | enforced | The recoverable closeout plan answers a judgment criterion to finish | pose-recoverable-closeout-plan |\n| `ready-from-absent-blockers` | enforced | Absence of a known blocker is presented as proven independence | pose-phase-scoped-readiness |\n| `stale-preview-authorizes-apply` | enforced | A start previewed before a restricting request is applied after it | pose-governed-effect-enforcement |\n| `code-change-keeps-judgment` | enforced | The reviewed code changes and every criterion still reads as equivalent, so the old judgment is reused | pose-material-equivalence-reuse |\n| `minimal-surface-skips-trace` | enforced | A done spec declares the minimal surface to drop its requirement trace | pose-progressive-spec-surface |\n| `stale-assessment-reused` | enforced | The assessed component changes and the old assessment still reads as fresh | pose-adaptive-assessment-freshness |\n| `unpinned-premise-trigger-reads-current` | enforced | A premise trigger without a pin can never go stale and nothing says so | pose-assumption-validity-scope |\n| `calendar-ttl-as-premise-trigger` | enforced | An arbitrary expiry date is accepted as the material trigger of a premise | pose-assumption-validity-scope |\n| `unobserved-falsifier-reads-uncontradicted` | enforced | An unbound legacy index cannot prove that a falsifier check was never observed | pose-falsifier-reconsideration |\n| `parity-row-cites-an-unrelated-test` | known-gap | A launcher parity row names a real but unrelated `pose delegate` command and an existing test that does not exercise the capability, and the parity check passes; the check proves existence, review of the cited tests proves coverage | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n| `imported-fragment-completes-a-replaced-command` | known-gap | A usage or error string assembles a removed command from a constant of another package of the module, which the active-document check reads as a gap; review of assembled messages is the defence | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n| `cgo-preamble-text-reaches-usage` | known-gap | Operator text written as a C string in a cgo preamble reaches a usage surface; the Go reader sees a comment, not a string | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n| `later-removal-hides-a-later-touch` | delegated | A later removal satisfies an earlier spec's claim because the history it is judged on omits that spec's change after the removal — change sets in ID order, a merge, root or type-change touch, a failed or shallow read, a recorded report too wide to read whole or a history directory that cannot be listed, a replace ref or graft (`cli/delivery_later_removal_history_test.go:TestLaterRemovalHistoryShapes`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_gaps_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundTwo`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_raw_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundThree`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_raw_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundFive`) | pose-delivery-later-removal |\n| `rename-read-as-removal` | delegated | A rename, or a path spelled as a pathspec, is taken for the declared deletion (`cli/delivery_later_removal_history_test.go:TestLaterRemovalHistoryShapes`) | pose-delivery-later-removal |\n| `recorded-commit-is-an-option` | delegated | A change set read from a recorded report names a Git option or a tag where a commit belongs (`cli/delivery_later_removal_history_test.go:TestLaterRemovalHistoryShapes`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_raw_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundThree`) | pose-delivery-later-removal |\n| `peer-removal-stands-for-a-member` | delegated | A review subject digests a removed path from a peer's accepted removal while another observing member — sorted later, sharing a commit, or reduced into the peer's set — has none, whatever action or rename it observed the path with (`pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestReviewSubjectReadsALaterRemovalFromItsWitness`, `pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestMilestoneSubjectRemovalHoldsForEveryMember`) | pose-review-subject-later-removal |\n| `retained-child-skips-its-verification` | delegated | A milestone seals over a done member whose own review verification no longer retains its approval — revoked federated trust, lost history, a later negative review (`pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestRetainedChildFollowsItsVerification`, `pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestMilestoneSealRetainsADoneChildsApprovedReview`) | pose-review-subject-later-removal |\n| `run-pattern-names-no-test` | delegated | A validation check's `-run` alternative names a test that no longer exists, or never did, and the check passes on Go's exit 0 — through `-run=`, a build-excluded or ignored file, a vendored or nested-module declaration, a benchmark or a name Go does not run (`cli/validation_matrix_patterns_test.go:TestDeadRunPatternGuardFollowsGoSelection`, `cli/validation_matrix_patterns_test.go:TestValidationMatrixRunPatternsNameExistingTests`); a non-plain pattern passes only when listed with its reason | pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns |\n| `removal-witness-outlives-its-history` | delegated | A stale index keeps counting a removal after a later touch, through a merge, a rewritten history or a shallow clone that lost the touch (`pose/removal_witness_freshness_test.go:TestLaterTouchRefusesTheWitness`, `pose/removal_witness_freshness_test.go:TestShallowHistoryRefusesTheWitness`) | pose-removal-witness-freshness |\n| `parent-outlives-a-rejected-child` | delegated | A milestone or roadmap stays approved over a child's later rejection, through retention, a sealed cycle, a replaced approval or a forged `replaces` (`pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestParentApprovalFollowsAChildsRejection`, `pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestChildCycleEndsInARefusal`, `pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestForgedReplacementRetiresNothing`, `pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestLegacyCoordinatedMatchingFollowsLineage`) | pose-review-approval-follows-children |\n| `go-check-ran-no-test` | delegated | A `go test` check selects nothing and passes on Go's exit 0, through a flag spelling, a flag's value read as a flag, or a package without test files (`cli/validate_empty_go_checks_test.go:TestValidateRefusesAGoCheckThatRanNoTest`, `cli/validate_empty_go_checks_test.go:TestGoTestSelection`); a check outside the plain grammar passes unjudged, and a test printing a result line can still mislead it | pose-validate-refuses-empty-go-checks |\n| `request-opened-after-preview-transfers` | delegated | A request opened after a transfer preview is moved with the spec (`pose/spec_transfer_actions_test.go:TestTransferRefusesARequestOpenedAfterThePreview`) | pose-transfer-preserves-obligations |\n\n| `deleted-reservation-resets-quota` | delegated | Deleting a reservation and receipt makes a surviving run stop consuming quota | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n| `witness-bundle-filter-hides-loss` | delegated | Editing a witness bundle makes scoped readers skip its corruption | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n| `window-erases-rerun` | delegated | Moving a prior run outside the time window turns a rerun into a first attempt | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n| `canned-executor-approval-proves-cognition` | delegated | A complete canned approval from a trusted local command is presented as proof of review cognition or a vendor receipt (`cli/delegated_review_capability_test.go:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityCannedApprovalDisclosesItsLimits` guards disclosure; the engine cannot detect canned judgments) | pose-delegated-review-capability |\n| `oversized-writer-publishes-unreadable-run` | delegated | A writer reports completion for a run its bounded reader immediately refuses | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
