{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --short; nl -ba POSE.md | sed -n '350,359p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go | sed -n '105,127p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"git status --short; nl -ba POSE.md | sed -n '350,359p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go | sed -n '105,127p'\"","aggregated_output":"   350\t- `new-knowledge` — creates an artifact in [`.pose/knowledge/`](.pose/knowledge/) from [`.pose/templates/knowledge.md`](.pose/templates/knowledge.md) with mandatory frontmatter (`type`, `owner`, `sensitivity`, `created_at`, `last_reviewed_at`, `expires_at`). Computes `expires_at` from the TTL (default 30d, max 90d).\n   351\t- `validate` — runs the declarative matrix in [`validation-matrix.json`](.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json): per-stack checks, per-module overrides, severity (`required`/`optional`) and mode (`strict`/`tolerant`). `--json-out`/`--junit`/`--sarif <path>` (`--json <path>` still works as a deprecated alias of `--json-out <path>`) emit the versioned structured result (schema 1) from one canonical model: stable check IDs (`<module>/<stack>/<name>`), command metadata, timing, severity, distinguishable outcomes (`pass|fail|error|skipped` — infra failures never masquerade as check failures), deterministic skip reasons, bounded captured output and secret redaction (configured env values only; inherited environment never enters the result). Text output stays authoritative; machine formats are additive. POSE-specific semantics survive the JUnit/SARIF projections via documented extensions (classname suffix / `pose/*` properties).\n   352\t  **Runtime guardrails:** every check runs under a timeout (`timeoutSeconds` per check, `defaults.timeoutSeconds`, safe default 600s) and an output ceiling (`defaults.maxOutputBytes`, default 1 MiB); breaching either terminates the process group and records the explicit state (`limit_state: timeout|output-limit`). Checks marked `isolation: \"required\"` never run locally — they are skipped with a machine-readable reason and exported by `--emit-plan <file>`: an execution-plan envelope binding project, spec, check plan, matrix digest, git HEAD and an approval slot to be stamped with an expiring execution identity before the Harness may run it.\n   353\t  **Changed scope:** `--changed-from <rev> [--changed-to <rev>]` selects the minimum safe module set deterministically — modules containing changed files (tracked and untracked), transitive dependents via `dependsOn` edges in [`module-metadata.json`](.pose/indexes/module-metadata.json), and policy widening (criticality `high` always runs). Changed names are read NUL-delimited and a rename names both its source and its destination. Each changed file selects its most specific owning module, every module enclosing that owner (the root module encloses them all), every module beneath it (a gitlink or replaced directory changes what lies under it), and every module whose declared `dependsOn` contains it, lies beneath it or is the root `.`, even after that dependency is deleted. A file no module owns selects the root module. Module metadata that does not decode stops the selection (a full run under `--carry`, an error under `--changed-from`). A change outside every module runs every module that does not declare `\"selfContained\": true` in its metadata (uncertainty prefers safe execution; the declaration states that the module's checks read only its own directory and its `dependsOn` modules); unselected checks are recorded as skipped with the selection reason and `--explain` prints every decision. Revisions are confined to a safe grammar; without the flags, full validation is unchanged.\n   354\t\n   355\t  **Carried checks:** `--carry --json-out <results_path>` refreshes the canonical result instead of rerunning the whole matrix. It uses the current canonical result as its base when the base is comparable: same schema, mode, matrix digest and `engine_version` (the engine version plus the VCS revision the binary was built from; a build of a modified tree never carries), unfiltered, not cancelled (a signal cancels the whole run, even an all-carried one), recorded `material_clean` (it validated an unchanged working copy of its own head: no tracked or untracked unignored material changed and HEAD did not move while it ran, as its reflog and every submodule's reflog show; mode changes count whatever `core.fileMode` says, and every submodule must hold its recorded commit with no nested submodule, checked both before the plan is read and when the run ends; a spec whose material the engine cannot compute stays unavailable in any clean run and does not refuse the base), with its `git_head` an ancestor of `HEAD`, a clean material working copy now, a case-sensitive filesystem with no case-folded directory on the path to a module or a dependency, no module reached through a symlink or sharing its directory with another module, no tracked symlink whose path or target lies in a module other than the root or in a declared `dependsOn` (or whose target leaves the repository), every submodule's tree included (a submodule that is not checked out or has nested submodules refuses), no declared dependency outside the repository or written as an unclean path or resolving through a symlink (tracked or ignored), only ASCII module and dependency paths, no index entry marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree, and no check id defined twice, and working module metadata equal to HEAD's. Changed names are read with every gitlink shown, whatever the Git configuration. The head is pinned before planning, and a run whose HEAD moved records its material bindings as unavailable. It runs the modules the changed-scope rules select between the base head and `HEAD`; the canonical result file and the derived administrative records that material bindings ignore (data files that are still regular files in the derived-record directories under `.pose/`: indexes, results, state, assessments and review records; the validation matrix stays material) are not changes. A module whose checks are not all in the base also runs. Every other check keeps the base result, its outcome included, and records `carried_from` (the head it ran at, kept through chained carries) and `carried_generated_at`; the delivery index reads that head for the result, so evidence freshness judges the commit a carried check really observed. A carried failure still fails the run. Any unmet condition runs everything, and `carry.reason` says why. `carry` records the base, the number of changed files and each selected module's reason, and `counts.carried` the reused checks. `--carry` does not combine with `--module`, `--stack`, `--workspace`, `--root-only`, `--changed-from` or `--changed-to`.\n   356\t\n   357\t  **Concurrency:** checks run up to `--jobs <n>` at a time (default: half the cores, bounded by available memory at about 1.5 GiB per check and by 8); results are reported and recorded in matrix order, whatever order they finish in, and the report records `jobs` and `wall_seconds`. `--jobs 1` and `--verbose` run one at a time. A check marked `exclusive: true` runs with nothing else running: earlier checks finish first, so its `when` can depend on them, which a concurrent check's cannot — a check's `when` is read as it starts. The run ends with its wall time beside the sum of its checks and the slowest checks. An interrupt or SIGTERM stops every running check's process group (on Windows, its process) and starts nothing more; those checks are recorded with `limit_state: cancelled`, the run is `fail` and exits 1, and a second signal acts at once. A default `--jobs` follows the cgroup's memory headroom and CPU quota where there is one.\n   358\t\n   359\t  **Empty Go checks:** a `go test` check that selects tests with `-run` or `-skip` and exits 0 fails with `limit_state: no-tests` when Go's result lines report every package as having run nothing, since Go exits 0 when a pattern selects nothing. A check over several packages passes when any of them reports running tests. The rule reads Go's summary and is no proof that a test ran; only a plain form is judged — packages, then `-run`, `-skip`, `-count`, `-timeout`, `-parallel`, `-cpu`, `-outputdir`, `-v`, `-short`, `-failfast`, `-race`, `-cover`, `-covermode`, `-coverpkg`, `-tags` and `-p` — and any other flag, `-args`, `--`, a positional argument after the packages or quoted `GOFLAGS` leaves a check with Go's own outcome.\n   105\t\t// copy that differed from its head proves nothing about that head.\n   106\t\tif !base.MaterialClean {\n   107\t\t\treturn unused(\"the canonical result did not validate a clean working copy of its head\")\n   108\t\t}\n   109\t\t// material_clean is the witness that the base validated its head. A spec\n   110\t\t// whose material the engine cannot compute is recorded unavailable in any\n   111\t\t// clean run, so an unavailable binding is not, by itself, a reason to\n   112\t\t// refuse; a run that was not clean has every binding unavailable and\n   113\t\t// material_clean false.\n   114\t\tif !materialWorktreeClean(root) {\n   115\t\t\treturn unused(\"the working copy differs from HEAD in material paths\")\n   116\t\t}\n   117\t\t// Selection is lexical: a module reached through a symlink aliases another\n   118\t\t// path, so its inputs cannot be told apart (review round 4, N9).\n   119\t\t// Two modules sharing one physical directory (a case alias on a\n   120\t\t// case-insensitive filesystem) alias each other too (review round 5, N13).\n   121\t\tif reason := aliasedModule(modules, filepath.EvalSymlinks, os.Stat); reason != \"\" {\n   122\t\t\treturn unused(\"%s\", reason)\n   123\t\t}\n   124\t\t// Lexical selection cannot see through aliases. Rather than chase every\n   125\t\t// alias form (review rounds 4–7, N9, N13, N16–N18), a carry needs a\n   126\t\t// case-sensitive filesystem and no tracked symlink that links a module\n   127\t\t// (other than the root) or a declared dependency with any other path.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nNo new implementation blocker was established. Approval remains blocked because the required artifact check and validation reruns could not be completed under the read-only boundary.\n\nTwo existing low-severity issues remain:\n\n- **N60:** `--carry --report` presents carried checks as executed commands without their original head or time. [validate.go:1623](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1520541794/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623)\n- **N61:** No dedicated fixture seals, verifies, and checks closeout over a carried record. This remains documented F1. [spec:261](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1520541794/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:261)\n\nFocused CLI tests passed, including a race-enabled run. The delivery parser test, build, and focused vet checks also passed. The full validation attempts were interrupted after the sandbox refused new build directories. The artifact check was stopped because its success path refreshes the delivery index. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\nRules applied during review: mixed Go feature and documentation change; review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. No UI or infrastructure rules applied.\n\nRemoving the unavailable-binding rejection appears consistent with R2: `material_clean` independently witnesses the validated head, while an uncomputable spec binding remains unavailable. The remaining explicit assumption is that module input declarations are accurate.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N60\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1623,\n      \"summary\": \"validationSummaryOf includes carried checks in executed Commands and renders their old outcomes and durations without carried_from or carried_generated_at. A newly dated --carry --report therefore misrepresents reused observations as commands executed by this run. This is existing follow-up F2.\",\n      \"action\": \"Exclude carried checks from executed Commands and label reused results with their original head and timestamp.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N61\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\",\n      \"line\": 261,\n      \"summary\": \"The delivery parser directly tests carried head and timestamp, but there is no dedicated end-to-end fixture sealing a review bundle, verifying it, and checking closeout over a carried record. This is existing follow-up F1.\",\n      \"action\": \"Add a disposable-repository integration fixture exercising seal, verify, and closeout-check over a carried record, including rejection of an unsuitable carried head.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1621-1636 still includes carried commands and omits carry provenance; tracked as F2 at spec line 262.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N42\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1621-1636; the report projection still lacks a CarriedFrom branch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N44\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still projects reused observations as executed commands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R16-N51\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636; existing F2 remains open.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N53\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636; no carried head or timestamp is rendered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N54\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Spec line 261 explicitly retains F1; delivery_validation_run_test.go:7 tests parsing only, and the subject-wide carry search found no dedicated seal/verify/closeout fixture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R18-N55\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 confirms the unchanged report-provenance defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R18-N56\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Spec line 261 retains the missing end-to-end carried-record coverage; the focused delivery parser test passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R19-N55\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Implementer-note reference to F2: validate.go:1623-1636 still omits carried provenance from reports.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R19-N56\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Implementer-note reference to F1: spec line 261 retains the end-to-end coverage gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R21-N57\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"POSE.md:355, locales/pt-BR/POSE.md and both embedded manual copies now explicitly state that an uncomputable material binding alone does not refuse a clean base, matching validate_carry.go:105-113.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R21-N58\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F2 remains at validate.go:1623-1636 and spec line 262.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R21-N59\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F1 remains explicitly open at spec line 261; direct parser coverage does not exercise seal, verification, or closeout.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the complete implementation diff, R1-R10, D1-D3, the ADR, argument incompatibilities, base comparability and cancellation, material cleanliness at both endpoints, HEAD and submodule movement witnesses, hidden index entries, alias and case-fold refusal, dependency and nested-module selection, administrative exclusions, duplicate and absent check handling, chained provenance, carried failures and counts, delivery parsing, reporting, help, translated and embedded manuals, regression tests, and relevant governance rules and adversarial-corpus documentation. Ran focused CLI tests normally and with the race detector, the delivery parser test, focused vet, and build successfully. Resolved the scope context, ran suggest-review and recurrence-check. Attempted both required validation commands and artifact-check but did not obtain completed passes. Confirmed git status remained clean. No additional implementation defect was established.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined R2, the unavailable-binding removal, cleanliness and movement witnesses, and the explicit selfContained declaration. Clean-head eligibility is independent of whether an individual spec binding is computable. Accurate module input declarations remain an explicit accepted design assumption. Independent full validation remains unresolved because of sandbox restrictions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined silent carried entries, dispatcher exclusion, ordered counting, cancellation finalization and signal handling. The focused Carry/ChangedScope/Validate/Material/Cancellation tests also passed with -race.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The JSON additions are optional, legacy results retain run-level head and time, and carried results use their original head and time. The direct delivery parser test passed independently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected incompatible flags, canonical-path requirements, revision confinement, malformed metadata, unavailable bases, duplicate IDs and conservative fallback reasons. Focused negative fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N61\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Delivery parsing is covered, while the dedicated carried-record seal/verify/closeout composition remains an owned low-severity coverage gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N60\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Structured carry provenance and fallback reasons are present, but the report projection loses provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed additive schema fields, unchanged legacy parsing, the opt-in CLI flag, and shared changed-scope behavior. No incompatible public contract change was established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined selection, full-run fallbacks, chained provenance, failure preservation, counts and cancellation. Focused normal and race-enabled tests, delivery parsing, build and vet passed. This does not represent a completed independent full-matrix run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 preserves observations rather than inventing new executions; D2 uses whole-matrix and engine identity to avoid per-check cache contracts; D3 keeps external-change exemptions explicit. The ADR records the structural evidence-reuse contract. The cheapest misleading shortcut is promoting a reused observation to the current head; carried_from propagation and the parser regression prevent that locally, while N61 records the missing composed proof.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"D1 explicitly rests on R3, R4 and R7 and requires preserving the original observation through carrying and delivery consumption; the added ADR records that contract and its alternatives.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the runtime with English, pt-BR and embedded manuals and help. All four manuals describe the removed unavailable-binding rejection correctly. The spec explicitly retains F1 and F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N60\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fallback reasons and selection explanations are actionable, but generated reports still misdescribe carried checks as executed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N61\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1-R10 have direct code and focused fixture support. End-to-end proof that R7 remains correct through review sealing, verification and closeout remains the explicitly documented F1 gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation stays within canonical result carrying, shared changed-scope selection, additive provenance, delivery parsing and matching documentation. No unrelated refactor was established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined revision grammar before Git use, path confinement, lexical and physical alias checks, submodule handling, hidden index entries and conservative refusal. No new dependency or secret exposure was found in the changed implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module selection and comparing the whole matrix and engine is smaller than introducing per-check input hashing or a separate cache. The added refusal checks defend lexical attribution. The choice would need reconsideration if instances cannot accurately declare cross-module inputs or require carrying across matrix or engine changes.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Attempted; emitted repository-wide orphan warnings. Stopped after source inspection confirmed that its success path refreshes the delivery index, which conflicts with the immutable-checkout boundary. No completed pass is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed structure evidence and independently inspected the design; did not run an assessment that could write in the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Discovery writes assessment/state artifacts. No writable scratch checkout was available.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment persists its integration matrix. Used sealed integration evidence and independent boundary inspection instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic\\\\(' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_results.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_validation_run.go\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment writes its report. A direct marker scan found none in these changed production files; existing residuals remain explicitly owned in F1 and F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion requires the recorded and verified review conclusion. This review does not record an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Depends on POSE recording and verifying this review conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved backend-go rules and the review workflow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Attempted through go -C pose-mcp run ./cmd/pose validate --strict and interrupted after the sandbox refused new Go build directories. The evidence ref is the previously sealed pass, not a successful independent rerun. Required gate completion remains unresolved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Attempted through go -C pose-mcp run ./cmd/pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp. Cancellation produced exit 1 with 54 passes and 179 cancelled errors. The evidence ref is the previously sealed pass; no independent full-matrix pass is claimed. Focused CLI tests, race-enabled focused tests, delivery parser test, build and focused vet passed separately.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
